{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794410979,"nonce":"ih3UpU9y/cTtkiMZPc5OOPb9gx8=","message":"Shared values are built: `#[hxn::interface(shared)]`.\n\nA handle of a shared interface holds an `Arc\u003cT\u003e`, so it is one share. The\nadapters open it as `Handle\u003cArc\u003cT\u003e\u003e` and every receiver is a shared borrow.\n\n- Parameters: `\u0026T` (the value) and `Arc\u003cT\u003e` (a share, cloned by the adapter),\n  and `Option` of either. `\u0026Arc\u003cT\u003e` and `\u0026mut T` are refused.\n- Results: `T`, which the adapter puts in an `Arc`, or `Arc\u003cT\u003e` as it is, and\n  `Option` of either. `Method.returns_arc` records which.\n- `\u0026mut self`, `self` by value and a typed receiver (`self: Box\u003cSelf\u003e`) are\n  refused. The last was read as `self` by value before; it is refused for\n  every interface now.\n- Each shared interface gets `same`, `weak`, `weak_upgrade` and `weak_close`\n  exports, `same(other)` and `weak()` on its Haxe class, and a class\n  `\u003cInterface\u003eWeak` with `upgrade()` and `close()`. `same(null)` is false.\n- `Arc\u003cT\u003e` of an interface not marked shared is refused, so a library cannot\n  share by accident what Haxe would treat as owned.\n\nFixture: `Pot` (shared) and `Player`, which keeps a share, in\n`tests/counter/core`; checked by `shared()` in `haxe/Generated.hx`.\n\nWeighed: whether `\u0026Arc\u003cT\u003e` should be accepted so a library can decide whether\nto clone. A clone is one increment and `Arc\u003cT\u003e` says what happens, so no.\n\nOpen:\n- `Rc`, for values that stay on one thread. A collector finalizes on whatever\n  thread it runs, so a handle's value must be `Send`.\n- A shared interface cannot be consumed (`self` by value). `Arc::try_unwrap`\n  would make that fail at run time depending on who else holds a share.\n- A weak reference has no `same`.\n- Not run on wasm or Emscripten, as nothing generated is yet.","files":null}]}